{"kind":"artifact","text":"The serving page stops describing a disagreement that no longer exists, and starts describing the one that does. Exact clean pushed head 128132f23c3ea13e7b0ed93e33735f6181531c92; tree unchanged from 9d3e6483, checkout clean, origin matching. Under planner's child 467ad483 and my promise 5ee01d7b.\n\nTHREE THINGS IT SAID THAT WERE FALSE AT THIS HEAD, and one that was false before it.\n\nIt said the two surfaces disagree knowingly about an untrustworthy record — that gs fails closed and the adapter treats it as no resident. That was the defect this head fixes, so the sentence had to go with it. Both now fail closed, and the page says what still differs: gs refuses the command, the adapter refuses the one call and keeps its attachment and session, so repairing the record is the whole recovery.\n\nIt said an untrusted record stopped every durable act. It does not: gs --server - reads no record at all and is the deliberate way past. That was wrong before this head too, and I would rather record that than let the correction look like a consequence of the change.\n\nIt said a hard-killed resident makes durable acts refuse. True of gs, not of the adapter, which folds locally and marks the result degraded — because there the record still reads as a good one and what is gone is the service, not the record. Conflating those two failures is exactly the confusion this lane is about.\n\nIt omitted that the adapter names gs --server - as a third recovery beside repairing and removing, which matters because the adapter has no flags of its own.\n\nWHAT IS ADDED. That the record is judged on every durable act rather than once per session, and read once more before any fall back to the local fold — the two properties the implementation now has and a reader could not have learned from this page.\n\nGATES, from runs I watched exit at this exact head. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 35 packages, 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached — internal/docset uncached at 172.454s, cmd/gs 318.689s, cmd/gitseq-mcp 206.823s. npm test 87 pass, 0 fail after npm ci in this worktree; the first run failed five files on a missing node_modules, which was the worktree and not this change. gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0; git diff --check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"128132f23c3ea13e7b0ed93e33735f6181531c92","path":"docs/reference/gs/serve.md"}}